Like what if they binge,

258
00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.520
but they never purge, they never fast,

259
00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.680
or run 10 miles afterward?

260
00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.360
Well, that shifts the clinical picture entirely

261
00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.440
to the third major condition in the guide,

262
00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.200
which is binge eating disorder.

263
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.280
Code F50.81.

264
00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.000
Yes.

265
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.160
It is defined as recurrent binge eating,

266
00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.880
accompanied by a profound sense of loss of control

267
00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.200
and marked intense distress.

268
00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.400
And like bulimia,

269
00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.560
this has to occur at least weekly for three months.

270
00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.640
But the guide hammers home the main point

271
00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.000
with absolute certainty.

272
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.720
There are NO compensatory behaviors.

273
00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.320
That absence of compensation

274
00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:07.280
is the whole defining separator from bulimia.

275
00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:07.780
Right.

276
00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.440
The individual experiences the overwhelming compulsion,

277
00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:13.920
the complete loss of control during the binge,

278
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.280
but the cycle just stops there.

279
00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:18.080
They endure the intense psychological pain,

280
00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:20.560
the shame, and the physical discomfort of the binge

281
00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.520
without utilizing any physical mechanism to undo it.

282
00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.840
Which must be incredibly distressing.

283
00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:26.480
It is.

284
00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.240
And because the behavior is different,

285
00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:30.400
the underlying neurobiologies is different.

286
00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.840
Research actually suggests that binge eating disorder

287
00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.960
is often linked to a deficit in dopamine receptors.

288
00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:37.840
Oh really?

289
00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.240
Yeah.

290
00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:40.880
The brain just isn't getting enough natural reward signals

291
00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.080
from everyday life,

292
00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:45.760
so it seeks out massive quantities of highly palatable food

293
00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:47.920
to basically force a dopamine spike.

294
00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:49.280
That makes perfect sense.

295
00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.080
And the treatment protocol reflects that difference beautifully.

296
00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.480
The guide states the first line psychological treatments

297
00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.880
are enhanced CBT or interpersonal therapy.

298
00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.200
But the approved medication option

299
00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:00.800
listed for binge eating disorder

300
00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.120
is a drug called listex amphetamine.

301
00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:04.320
Now I looked this.

302
00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:08.000
A listex amphetamine is a central nervous system stimulant.

303
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.320
It is often used to treat ADHD.

304
00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.960
We just talked about using an SSRI antidepressant

305
00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.120
for bulimia to stabilize mood,

306
00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.600
but here we are using a literal stimulant

307
00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.640
for binge eating.

308
00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.680
Because a stimulant targets the exact dopamine deficit

309
00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:22.640
we just discussed.

310
00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:25.760
By stimulating the central nervous system,

311
00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.800
listex amphetamine increases the availability

312
00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.720
of dopamine and norepinephrine in the brain's synapses.

313
00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.640
So it's feeding the brain what it's looking for.

314
00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.200
Exactly.

315
00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.600
It basically wakes up the prefrontal cortex,

316
00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.080
the part of the brain responsible for executive function

317
00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:40.960
and impulse control.

318
00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:44.400
When the brain has a steady adequate supply of dopamine

319
00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:48.000
from the medication, the overwhelming impulsive drive

320
00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.600
to seek out a massive food reward is dramatically reduced.

321
00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.240
To me, this just proves the absolute necessity

322
00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.240
of accurate clinical diagnosis.

323
00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.040
Without a doubt.

324
00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:58.960
I mean, if you have someone who is binging

325
00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.880
and you don't take the time to use this framework

326
00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.040
to figure out if they are compensating or not,

327
00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.640
the results could be disastrous.

328
00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:05.440
Oh, completely.

329
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.040
If you misdiagnose bulimia as binge eating disorder

330
00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.280
and you hand a central nervous system stimulant

331
00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.200
to a patient who is actively purging,

332
00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.480
you might severely spike their anxiety,

333
00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.680
increase their heart rate,

334
00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.000
and actually accelerate the compulsion to purge.

335
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:20.320
Wow.

336
00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.440
Treating the wrong disorder with the wrong med

337
00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.400
just wouldn't work.

338
00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:27.440
Precision medicine really requires precise categorization.

339
00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.080
It does.

340
00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.160
The clinical lines drawn by these separators

341
00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:33.120
dictate the chemical and psychological tools you use

342
00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.800
to literally save someone's life.

343
00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:35.120
Okay.

344
00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.600
So we've covered weight, we've covered compensation,

345
00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.800
but earlier we talked about a third separator, body image.

346
00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:41.920
Yes, the third pillar.

347
00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:42.640
Right.

348
00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.000
Up until now, anorexia, bulimia, and binge eating disorder

349
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.480
all feature this massive overwhelming distress

350
00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:52.320
about body shape, weight, or an intense fear of fatness.

351
00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.720
The patient's self-worth is entirely tethered

352
00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.000
to their physical form,

353
00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.160
but what if an eating disorder has absolutely nothing

354
00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.200
to do with body image?

355
00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.840
Which brings us to the fourth diagnosis in this prep guide,

356
00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.200
Avoidant Restrictive Food Intake Disorder,

357
00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.280
commonly known as ARFID.

358
00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.520
Code F50.82.

359
00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:14.240
The guide defines ARFID as food avoidance or restriction

360
00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.120
that leads to significant nutritional deficiency,

361
00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:20.000
weight loss, or dependence on supplemental feeding.

362
00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:21.920
Now, on the surface,

363
00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:25.040
if a patient walks into a clinic severely underweight

364
00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.800
because they are avoiding food,

365
00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.800
it sounds exactly like anorexia.

366
00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:29.520
Right.

367
00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.080
Physically, the presentation can be identical.

368
00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.480
The malnutrition can be just as severe,

369
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:37.200
but the psychological engine driving the starvation

370
00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.800
is fundamentally different.

371
00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:42.400
And the prep guide explicitly states this separator.

372
00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:45.440
The restriction in ARFID is not driven by body image

373
00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.800
or a fear of gaining weight.

374
00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.840
There is zero body image disturbance whatsoever.

375
00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.400
None.

376
00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:52.880
So what actually drives someone to stop eating

377
00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.960
to the point of clinical malnutrition,

378
00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.480
if not a desire to be thin?

379
00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:00.320
The guide identifies three specific drivers for ARFID.

380
00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.000
First, it can be entirely about

381
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.600
the sensory qualities of the food.

382
00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:04.240
Like the texture.

383
00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:05.840
Yeah, the texture, the smell, the temperature,

384
00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.760
or even just the look of the food

385
00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:10.000
is so overwhelming to the nervous system

386
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.160
that the brain registers it as intolerable.

387
00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.920
Okay, what's the second driver?

388
00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:17.280
Second, it can be driven by an intense fear

389
00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.200
of an aversive consequence.

390
00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:22.400
Meaning, the person is terrified that if they swallow,

391
00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:24.160
they will choke or they will vomit.

392
00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.160
Oh, wow. And the third.

393
00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:29.200
Third, it can simply be a profoundly low interest

394
00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:30.320
in eating altogether.

395
00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:33.520
The fundamental biological drive for hunger

396
00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:35.760
just isn't registering in the brain.

397
00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.600
The guide also notes that ARFID

398
00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.920
is seen very frequently in children, right?

399
00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:40.880
Yes, very often.

400
00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.040
Imagine a child who experienced

401
00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:45.040
a traumatic choking incident.

402
00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.640
Their developing brain creates

403
00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.040
a massive hardwired association

404
00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.600
between the act of eating and mortal danger.

405
00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.280
They aren't avoiding food

406
00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.360
because they want to fit into a smaller clothing sign.

407
00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:56.480
Right, obviously not.

408
00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:58.160
Their nervous system is screaming at them

409
00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.360
that the act of swallowing

410
00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:01.120
is a literal threat to their survival.

411
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.440
So what does this all mean?

412
00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.720
When I read this section,

413
00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:07.280
I realized ARFID sounds far more

414
00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.360
like a specific severe phobia

415
00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.640
than what culture traditionally

416
00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:11.920
calls an eating disorder.

417
00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:13.760
That's a very accurate way to look at it.

418
00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:14.960
It's like being terrified

419
00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:17.040
of getting trapped in a building's elevator

420
00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.800
rather than hating the architecture

421
00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:19.920
of the building itself.

422
00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:23.120
The restriction is a desperate safety mechanism

423
00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.680
against choking or sensory overload,

424
00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.360
not a weight control tactic.

425
00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.240
Exactly. The avoidance is a protective instinct

426
00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.960
that has just gone into pathological overdrive.

427
00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.720
And because the driver of the disease

428
00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:37.840
is a phobia or a sensory processing issue,

429
00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:39.200
the treatment diverges completely

430
00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.800
from the other disorders we've discussed.

431
00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:41.680
How so?

432
00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.520
The guide states that the first line treatment

433
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:47.040
for ARFID is nutritional rehabilitation

434
00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.760
combined with behavioral and family work.

435
00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.680
You do not use enhanced CBT

436
00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.840
to challenge their beliefs about their body weight.

437
00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:54.960
Because they already know

438
00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.320
their body weight isn't the problem.

439
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.360
Precisely.

440
00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.280
Instead, clinicians use exposure

441
00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.640
and behavioral therapies

442
00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:04.240
to slowly, safely desensitize the nervous system

443
00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:06.080
to the sensory experience of food.

444
00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.920
It is entirely about retraining

445
00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:09.440
the brain's threat response.

446
00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:11.200
Like, a therapist might spend weeks

447
00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:13.120
just having a patient sit in the same room

448
00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.000
as a certain food.

449
00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.760
Then touching it.

450
00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:16.720
Then smelling it.

451
00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.120
Slowly proving to the amygdala

452
00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.960
that the texture or the act of swallowing

453
00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:22.160
will not result in death.

454
00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.080
It's slow, methodical work.

455
00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.160
Well, we've covered a tremendous amount of ground today

456
00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.280
pulling apart this framework.

457
00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:28.160
Let's lock this in

458
00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.920
so you listening to this

459
00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.680
can take this clinical map with you.

460
00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.200
Okay, so we have three core separators

461
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.720
that define the major eating disorders.

462
00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.240
First is weight.

463
00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.960
The presence of significantly low weight

464
00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:40.000
is the clinical anchor

465
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.920
that separates anorexia from bulimia.

466
00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:42.720
Got it.

467
00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.000
Second is compensation.

468
00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.080
The presence or absence

469
00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.680
of commensatory behaviors

470
00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.440
like purging or extreme fasting

471
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.240
separates bulimia from binge eating disorder.

472
00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:52.880
And the third.

473
00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:54.320
Third is body image.

474
00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.480
The complete absence of body image fears

475
00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:59.120
or fat phobia separates ARFID

476
00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.160
from anorexia.

477
00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.680
By looking for the low weight,

478
00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.840
identifying the compensatory behaviors

479
00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.920
and assessing the body image drivers,

480
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.800
clinicians can cut through the behavioral chaos.

481
00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:11.200
They can pinpoint exactly what neural pathways

482
00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.440
and physiological crises they're dealing with.

483
00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:15.520
It brings order to what looks like chaos.

484
00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:16.960
And for you listening to this,

485
00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.520
why is keeping this medical framework in mind

486
00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:20.720
so valuable?

487
00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:21.840
Because understanding

488
00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.760
these exact clinical separators

489
00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:26.320
helps you cut through the cultural noise.

490
00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:27.760
It destroys the stereotype

491
00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:30.000
that eating disorders all look a certain way

492
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.760
or that they are merely an expression

493
00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:32.960
of extreme vanity.

494
00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:33.920
Which is so important.

495
00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:34.880
It allows you to view

496
00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.080
these incredibly complex agonizing conditions

497
00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.320
through a lens that is medically accurate

498
00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.600
and deeply empathetic.

499
00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:44.000
When you know the actual mechanisms

500
00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:44.960
of the suffering,

501
00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:46.240
whether it's a heart failing

502
00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:47.600
from a lack of electrolytes,

503
00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:50.160
a brain lacking the glucose to think

504
00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:52.800
or nervous system terrified of swallowing,

505
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.000
you can better understand

506
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.120
the immense reality

507
00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.720
of the people enduring it.

508
00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:58.560
It permanently shifts your perspective

509
00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.000
from casual judgment

510
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.080
to genuine clinical understanding.

511
00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:02.720
Absolutely.

512
00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.840
But before we wrap up today's deep dive,

513
00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:06.560
I want to leave you

514
00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.080
with a final thought to ponder.

515
00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.600
Something that builds

516
00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.040
right out of the source material

517
00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.080
and the treatment protocols

518
00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:12.880
we just analyzed.

519
00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:14.800
We noted earlier

520
00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:15.680
that when treating

521
00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:17.600
the exact same condition,

522
00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.840
anorexia adolescents respond best

523
00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:21.280
to family-based treatment.

524
00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.640
Right, where the family steps in

525
00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:23.760
as the executive function.

526
00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:24.480
Exactly.

527
00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:26.240
Meanwhile, adults respond best

528
00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.920
to enhanced CBT,

529
00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:29.120
where the individual is taught

530
00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.640
to tackle their own internal

531
00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.960
cognitive distortions independently.

532
00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.080
The clinical pathways

533
00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.320
to rewiring the brain diverge

534
00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.760
based entirely on the age

535
00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.520
and developmental stage of the patient.

536
00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:41.440
Which raises a truly fascinating

537
00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.880
question to explore on your own.

538
00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:44.800
How much does our age

539
00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.760
and the immediate structure

540
00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:46.880
